/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 189 0 R
/T (PCC \(Pearson Correlation Coefficient\) [Semantic Implement] Purpose: Measures linear correlation between the ground-truth image & the reconstructed image on a pixel or feature level. Why we used it \(as in Koide-Majima et al., 2024\): Used directly as the similarity function in the Bayesian posterior log-likelihood during reconstruction. Reflects voxel-level decoding accuracy and is directly tied to reconstruction performance. Interpretation: Values range from -1 \(perfect negative correlation\) to 1 \(perfect positive correlation\) | Higher PCC indicates better alignment )
/E (PCC \(Pearson Correlation Coefficient\) [Semantic Implement] Purpose: Measures linear correlation between the ground-truth image & the reconstructed image on a pixel or feature level. Why we used it \(as in Koide-Majima et al., 2024\): Used directly as the similarity function in the Bayesian posterior log-likelihood during reconstruction. Reflects voxel-level decoding accuracy and is directly tied to reconstruction performance. Interpretation: Values range from -1 \(perfect negative correlation\) to 1 \(perfect positive correlation\) | Higher PCC indicates better alignment )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
